## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server
├── app.ts                   ← builds the Koa app; separate from main.ts so tests can import it directly
├── config/env.ts            ← the only file that reads process.env
├── errors/app-error.ts      ← domain-agnostic error classes
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
└── features/<module>/
    ├── <module>.routes.ts              ← wires everything (manual DI)
    ├── commands/                       ← write-path command + handler
    ├── events/                         ← domain event classes
    ├── aggregates/                     ← aggregate root (replays events, tracks uncommitted)
    ├── projections/                    ← materialized read model
    ├── event-store/                    ← append-only event log
    ├── dto/                            ← request validation
    └── infrastructure/                 ← controller + outbox
```

## Event-Driven flow

```
POST /product  →  Controller  →  CreateProductHandler
                                   →  ProductAggregate.create(name)
                                   →  getUncommittedEvents()
                                   →  EventStore.append(id, type, events, expectedVersion)
                                   →  Outbox.enqueue(storedEvents)
                                   →  Projection.handleCreatedEvent(event)

GET  /product/:id  →  Controller  →  Projection.findById(id)  (never hits event store)

PATCH /product/:id  →  Controller  →  EventStore.getEvents(id)
                                    →  ProductAggregate.fromHistory(events)
                                    →  aggregate.updateName(newName)
                                    →  getUncommittedEvents()
                                    →  EventStore.append(...)
```

Writes go through the event store and rebuild state from events. Reads go directly to projections — fast, denormalized views.

